		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3349&amp;p=26637#p26637"><![CDATA[
1. Coordinates of the repeater or whatever else (in this case hotspot) the channel settings specifies<br>2. Distance to the channels with coordinates is displayed on the bottom line of the screen (if no distance is available, you will see --- km)<br>3. Does not have to matter, location can be set manually. Go to Radio Info menu, use down arrow 3 times and you can enter the latitude and longitude by numeric buttons, N/S  can be changed by arrows and E/W by SK2(?) + arrows (RT3s). Once you confirm with green button, the coordinates of the radio are set and the distances will be calculated<br>4. For radio WITH GPS, either you can set the coordinates manually before getting the position, or the GPS position will overwrite them and distance will be calculated accordingly<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4053">OK2MOP</a> — Mon Oct 02, 2023 8:01 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
